  carrying capacity: 191 to 191 agents over the last 100 ticks
  survivors: mean vision 3.72 (started 3.46), mean metabolism 1.46 (started 2.48)
  wealth: mean 14.9 at the start, 637.0 at the end; Gini 0.228 -> peak 0.350 at tick 12 -> 0.227
  wealth at the end: median 620, top tenth above 949, richest 984
  one agent per cell at every recorded tick: TRUE

  The population falls to what the landscape can feed and stays there.
  Who survives is not random: the far-sighted and the frugal, which is
  Epstein & Axtell's selection result. Inequality spikes while the poor
  are dying off and then settles: once the survivors are the survivors,
  wealth grows at a rate set by each one's vision and metabolism, so the
  wealth Gini converges on the Gini of those income rates.
